# AI Development Workflow (UnionHub)

Before writing or changing code, read and align with:

1. `docs/architecture.mermaid` — system boundaries and integrations
2. `docs/technical.md` — stack, modules, security, TDD commands
3. `tasks/tasks.md` — active task ID, acceptance criteria, test plan
4. `docs/status.md` — stable features, known pitfalls, last decisions
5. `CLAUDE.md` — repo-specific commands, production checklist, conventions

## Repositories of truth

| Area | Path |
|------|------|
| Backend | `api/` (NestJS 11, TypeORM, PostgreSQL) |
| Mobile | `apps/mobile/` (Expo 52, React Native) |
| Web / landing | `apps/web/`, landing as applicable |

Do not assume `app/` for the mobile client — use `apps/mobile/`.

## Test-driven development

1. Define behavior from task acceptance criteria.
2. Add or update failing tests first (backend: `*.service.spec.ts` next to services; mobile: Jest where applicable).
3. Implement minimal change; make tests pass.
4. Run targeted tests before claiming done (`cd api && npm test`, `cd apps/mobile && npm test`).

## Context recovery

When resuming after compaction or a new session, rehydrate with explicit references:

- `@docs/status.md` — pitfalls and current stability
- `@tasks/tasks.md` — what to implement now
- `@docs/technical.md` — module and security rules
- `@CLAUDE.md` — operational commands

## Delivery checklist

- [ ] Task ID noted in commit/PR description when applicable
- [ ] Migrations generated for schema changes (never `synchronize: true` in prod)
- [ ] i18n keys added to `apps/mobile/src/i18n/en.json` and `it.json` (dot notation)
- [ ] No secrets in commits; `.env` unchanged unless user requested
